Z||000000||kornholio||09-05-99||11:37 AM||||Sometimes this happens (70% of the time). Does it happen to anyone else?
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-99||12:34 PM||||Only when going into park? Could be the neutral start switch is bad and cutting power to something when it shouldn't.<p>If it was happening when stopping for whatever reason then I'd suspect the TCC solinoid, but you are already stopped......
Z||000002||K9||09-05-99||05:32 PM||||Check out the Haynes manua, It showes how to check the N/P switch. <br>Good luck.
Z||000003||kornholio||09-08-1999||03:59 AM||||My car doesn't stall anymore...I guess it needed a tune-up. I decided to change the air filter, spark plugs, wires, distributor cap and rotor. Now my Fiero idles at a fixed rpm and I've noticed a little more "spunk." I wonder if replacing all of those things were necessary to get that extra kick. I bought a Wells cap and rotor. Anyone heard of that name? The wires that I bought are Niehoff platinum. They were more expensive than the Accel super stocks, so does that mean they are better?||||reg||
Z||000004||DJRice||09-08-1999||02:47 PM||||Fresh plugs and related equipment will always add some spunk for a while.<P>More expensive does not always mean better.  However, platinum wires should be very conductive.  I just use standard 8mm wires that come with a lifetime warranty.  The best investment in that kind of tune up would be some good plugs and a cap and rotor that have the brass contacts, the brass last longer.  As for the plugs, it seems like everyone has a different opinion on plugs, I just use Bosch Platinum.||||reg||
